{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SessionLock"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","externalID":"s:6Yorkie11SessionLockP","title":"SessionLock","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SessionLock"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SessionLock"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sendable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A lease is taken per attachment, keyed by the API key, client key and document key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and held for the attachment’s lifetime. It matters only when a persistent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/DocStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is shared by more than one process: two sessions resuming the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"persisted document would both re-push the same un-acknowledged local changes."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Platform note","level":2,"anchor":"Platform-note"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Upstream’s default is built on the browser’s Web Locks API to keep two tabs apart,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and is documented there as a no-op outside a browser. iOS has no tabs, and an app is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a single process, so "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/NoopSessionLock","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the default here and matches upstream’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own non-browser behaviour."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The hazard is still reachable on Apple platforms when a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"persistent"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" store is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shared across processes — an app and its share extension or widget writing to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same App Group container. A caller who does that should supply an implementation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backed by cross-process coordination, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSFileCoordinator"},{"type":"text","text":" or a lock file."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/SessionLock\/acquire(name:)"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/sessionlock"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"},{"type":"conformingTypes","title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/NoopSessionLock"],"kind":"relationships"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/SessionLock"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Guards a store-backed document against being resumed by two sessions at once."}],"references":{"doc://Yorkie/documentation/Yorkie/SessionLock":{"url":"\/documentation\/yorkie\/sessionlock","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SessionLock","kind":"iden